# SAP transport cofiles and data files (K900001.DEV, R900001.DEV: the
# extension is the system ID) are binary R3trans containers, not text.
# Without this, git's text heuristic plus core.autocrlf=true silently
# CRLF-converts short, ASCII-looking cofiles on checkout and corrupts their
# length and bytes. Data files usually escape by containing NUL bytes;
# cofiles do not.
# Matched by name (K/R + six digits, optionally prefixed): git may match
# patterns case-insensitively, so an extension-only rule would catch .txt
# (and a [KR] class does not match there).
K[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].* -text -diff
*_K[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].* -text -diff
R[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].* -text -diff
*_R[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].* -text -diff
*.sh text eol=lf
